/*=============================================================================
    Battle Arena : LOCAL 2-Player Fighting Game (single board) w/ Board 2
                   acting as a live "reaction commentator" scoreboard.
    Target      : Nuvoton NUC140VE3AN (NuTiny / LB-002 Learning Board)
    Toolchain   : Keil uVision (ARM-ADS, armcc)

    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    DESIGN NOTE
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    All real gameplay (movement/attacks/HP/timer) still runs ENTIRELY on
    this board, same as before - no per-frame position syncing, so there
    is no lag/desync risk during actual play. What's new is a small set
    of lightweight, low-frequency EVENT packets sent to Board 2 so it can
    react like a commentator, plus a short handshake at the start so both
    boards begin the countdown together:

        1) READY HANDSHAKE (new)
           Both boards must have their own key 5 pressed before the
           countdown starts. Each board announces itself with
           CMD_PLAYER_READY the moment ITS key 5 is pressed, and waits
           until it has ALSO heard a CMD_PLAYER_READY from the other
           board before moving on.

        2) COUNTDOWN SYNC (new, and slowed down)
           Every countdown screen this board shows is also broadcast as
           a CMD_COUNTDOWN packet so Board 2 shows the same screen at
           roughly the same time. Timings were slowed down.

        3) LIVE COMMENTARY EVENTS (new, one-shot / low-rate only)
              CMD_HIT     data=1 boy got hit, data=2 girl got hit
              CMD_LOSING  data=1 boy <=30 HP,  data=2 girl <=30 HP
                          (sent ONCE, the moment HP first drops to <=30)
              CMD_IDLE    sent if ~4 seconds pass in battle with no hit
                          landed (repeats every ~4s while still idle)
           None of these carry position data and none of them are sent
           more than a few times a second at most, so this stays cheap.

        4) FINAL RESULT (unchanged from before)
              CMD_RESULT_BOY / CMD_RESULT_GIRL / CMD_GAME_OVER / CMD_RESTART

    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    !! KEYPAD BUDGET !! (unchanged from before)
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
        Girl (top row)    : 1=Left  2=Punch  3=Right   7=Special
        Boy  (middle row) : 4=Left  5=Punch  6=Right   9=Special
    Key 5 doubles as "I'm ready" ONLY while in the pre-match ready screen;
    once battle starts it's boy's punch as before, no conflict.
=============================================================================*/

